Package: twocpcont
Type: Package
Title: Noniterative Closed-Form Sample Size for Trials with Two
    Co-Primary Continuous Endpoints
Version: 0.1.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Gosuke", "Homma",
           email = "my.name.is.gosuke@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides a noniterative, closed-form sample size formula
    for two-group superiority clinical trials with two co-primary
    continuous endpoints under the known-variance assumption. The
    closed-form expression is derived by combining Plackett's identity
    with Gauss-Legendre quadrature for the correlation integral and two
    analytic Taylor linearizations of the resulting power equation. A
    conventional sequential-search method based on the bivariate normal
    distribution is also implemented for benchmarking. Two design
    summaries are also provided: the maximum reduction rate of the
    required sample size that correlation adjustment can achieve, and a
    threshold effect-size ratio above which the between-endpoint
    correlation changes the required sample size by at most a
    user-specified fraction.
